\pard\sb60\sa60 \par
\pard\sb120\sa120\fs22 {\\b Status: Active and Ongoing}\par
\pard\sb60\sa60 \par
\pard\sb120\sa120\fs22 This document is not finished. It is a record of a research process that is still in motion. The framework presented here will be challenged, revised, and expanded as new evidence and new domains are examined. Some of the claims made here may not survive that process. That is the point.\par
\pard\sb60\sa60 \par
\pard\sb120\sa120\fs22 The three contributions we believe are new have survived multiple rounds of adversarial mathematical testing. But surviving a test is not the same as being proven. We are actively seeking to disprove them. If you find a prior work that covers the same ground, we want to know. If you find a domain where the Orientation Theorem fails, we want to know that too.\par
\pard\sb60\sa60 \par
\pard\sb120\sa120\fs22 The next phase of this research involves moving from theoretical claims to empirical tests. We are building systems that apply the Interaction Field Equation in practice, logging every decision and outcome, and using that data to validate or falsify the predictions made here. The goal is not to be right. The goal is to find out what is actually true.\par
\pard\sb60\sa60 \par
\pard\sb120\sa120\fs22 {\\b Important Caveat:} The theorems and predictions presented in this essay are largely untested and unapplied in practice. The mathematical logic is internally consistent and has survived adversarial scrutiny, but internal consistency is not the same as empirical validation. Rigorous real-world testing across the domains described here has not yet been conducted. We believe the framework is sound. We do not yet know that it is. That distinction matters, and we state it plainly.\par
\pard\sb60\sa60 \par
\pard\sb120\sa120\fs22 {\\b In Progress:} Domain-specific reports are being developed for pharmaceutical R&D and supply chain logistics. These reports will operationalize the Orientation Theorem with concrete, testable predictions and implementation guidance.\par
\pard\sb60\sa60 \par
\pard\sb120\sa120\fs22 {\\b Planned:} We intend to submit the core claims to economists, complexity theorists, and mathematicians for independent review. This document will be updated with their responses, including critical ones.\par
